Third-party components and sources
==================================

This file records every third-party component the release names or depends on, the
licence it is distributed under upstream, and where that licence is stated. It does
not restate the licence texts; follow the source links.

The release vendors no third-party source code and bundles no third-party weights or
records. Where the mechanism depends on an external project, the code here points at
the project rather than copying it.

Models, recipes and comparators
-------------------------------

HunyuanVideo-1.5 (Tencent Hunyuan)
    Role     : the latent video diffusion transformer whose attention modules the
               mechanism privatises.
    Source   : https://github.com/Tencent-Hunyuan/HunyuanVideo-1.5
               https://huggingface.co/tencent/HunyuanVideo-1.5
    Licence  : Tencent Hunyuan Community License, as stated on the model card and in
               the upstream repository. Not redistributed here.

Swin-UMamba (Jiarun Liu and contributors)
    Role     : the state-space vessel-segmentation architecture the appearance branch
               follows.
    Source   : https://github.com/JiarunLiu/Swin-UMamba
    Licence  : Apache License 2.0, as stated in the upstream repository.

DP-LDMs (Michael F. Liu, Saiyue Lyu, Margarita Vinaroz and Mijung Park)
    Role     : the attention-module privatisation recipe the mechanism builds on.
    Source   : https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.15759
    Licence  : arXiv perpetual non-exclusive licence.

TD-MPC2 (Nicklas Hansen, Hao Su and Xiaolong Wang)
    Role     : the continuous-control world model reproduced as a comparator.
    Source   : https://github.com/nicklashansen/tdmpc2
    Licence  : MIT, as stated in the upstream repository.

